      <rules>
        <rule name="Mounted Archers" id="a062-6da0-9b88-d74b" hidden="false">
          <description>Hun riders can be equipped with composite bows or slings.


Their use imposes the same restrictions on these cavalry figures as they do on infantry (see the rulebook, p.45).</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Composite Bow" id="7e7f-1b3d-fe9a-4d77" hidden="false">
          <description>Hun warriors can be equipped with composite bows.


These have the same characteristics as an ordinary bow, but their range is 30” rather than 20”. 


Composite bows also don’t have a penalty for shooting at long range.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Alan Heavy Cavalry" id="7d47-d391-1bf1-3b93" hidden="false">
          <description>The Alans were the Huns’ allies during several campaigns 
and their heavy cavalry was deployed to great advantage.


Huns therefore have access to cataphracts.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Every Man A Rider" id="76a7-8582-781a-e4e0" hidden="false">
          <description>The Huns don’t have the usual 25% limit on mounted figures.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Inflammatory Approach" id="c4e2-9f28-808c-675e" hidden="false">
          <description>Hun cavalry can pick up torches and use them to start fires, in the same way as any infantry figure.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Lasso" id="cedd-00cc-6d9b-5d81" hidden="false">
          <description>All mounted Huns have a lasso. 


The lasso can only be used by a mounted figure.


On a roll of 6 to hit in melee, the lasso cancels the enemy’s attack.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </forceEntry>
  </forceEntries>
</catalogue>
